    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0675" n="573" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg573"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">883.05/529: Telegram (part air)</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Fish</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-02-08T10:00:00+02:00">February 8,
                            1935—10 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 11—12:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. Legation’s 4, January 25, 10 a.m. Egyptian Foreign Office in a note received
                    today requests that the American Government be good enough to expedite
                    Government reply to circular note No. 27, October 12, 1934.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
